{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})=4x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})=-6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}4x & -6y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection/015ed85c08ac0501dc450727e437229d0f766422ffb8fd983e84145ddf6f7748" :answer/id #uuid "6e55cb00-638f-520a-8498-b89993f51aeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection/489bbe24981be071fd4422606cf64ddfbe411bc93902cb827590d1c9e226e4fe" :answer/id #uuid "e783d05f-2fc3-5115-8661-58844887006c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection/4fef8c99fab59e84965a77f9daeaa9b35e4eabfb217e14a00739333e1ffcb3f8" :answer/id #uuid "b739c1d3-7ece-5955-8447-27b166d2513f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection/878b0a057c824c4ff1f6e81a133b75ead800cb168e8a0fcc475495b9814edeb2" :answer/id #uuid "f92d586a-84e1-55f9-b37b-df2b977fd1d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection/83c5889bf3d60822459b98b7c76bc575eeea0b139ad29da005ec107acfc19943" :answer/id #uuid "c2d9c58e-af98-5368-8b7d-91f69e3d20e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "37273e20-c281-533a-8df9-7bd71e25382b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163044/selection/489bbe24981be071fd4422606cf64ddfbe411bc93902cb827590d1c9e226e4fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-163044/selection/015ed85c08ac0501dc450727e437229d0f766422ffb8fd983e84145ddf6f7748" "q-163044/selection/489bbe24981be071fd4422606cf64ddfbe411bc93902cb827590d1c9e226e4fe" "q-163044/selection/4fef8c99fab59e84965a77f9daeaa9b35e4eabfb217e14a00739333e1ffcb3f8" "q-163044/selection/878b0a057c824c4ff1f6e81a133b75ead800cb168e8a0fcc475495b9814edeb2" "q-163044/selection/83c5889bf3d60822459b98b7c76bc575eeea0b139ad29da005ec107acfc19943"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163044" :question/id #uuid "86347eb1-d7e8-5d5a-b478-0a57c42a6dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163044" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+{y}^{3},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})=3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2(2) & 3(1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163044/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163044"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection/9fb26300cc36c742d06dec8a3fe99aefc8f61ef7897d2b2c6edb1740acadbde7" :answer/id #uuid "799582e5-f8ef-5727-9064-262ea9736abc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ x-y & -(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection/604c43c72eb13cece6fac83910472cc7480136273ab49f52c4ce4e22802835bc" :answer/id #uuid "15d312ba-0b0d-5fd9-a675-24172c80b279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection/d397a0179f1516ea65c153059e9025b21cea30644ba836a456177d2f4f0796ee" :answer/id #uuid "b068e577-95a8-53f4-b642-f15686168a0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2}y \\\\ -2(x-y) & 2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection/351755cf3cc3cbbcae5b0130ab75c21ac4535a59287d777a9f5d3faaa280c6dd" :answer/id #uuid "da23fd82-eeba-5726-977e-d84d081786c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & 2x \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection/91c0476a5995a101d065aa02f96bb2bd3bd8566e6f79430e165120e02def760d" :answer/id #uuid "db47963d-1476-5bc4-a619-a48ea073c291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & 2x \\\\ x-y & y-x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9877b7f3-ce64-54d5-b1a4-46b897ffabda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163097/selection/604c43c72eb13cece6fac83910472cc7480136273ab49f52c4ce4e22802835bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-163097/selection/9fb26300cc36c742d06dec8a3fe99aefc8f61ef7897d2b2c6edb1740acadbde7" "q-163097/selection/604c43c72eb13cece6fac83910472cc7480136273ab49f52c4ce4e22802835bc" "q-163097/selection/d397a0179f1516ea65c153059e9025b21cea30644ba836a456177d2f4f0796ee" "q-163097/selection/351755cf3cc3cbbcae5b0130ab75c21ac4535a59287d777a9f5d3faaa280c6dd" "q-163097/selection/91c0476a5995a101d065aa02f96bb2bd3bd8566e6f79430e165120e02def760d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163097" :question/id #uuid "506e4392-8367-5c22-bb2c-6ffe4b882c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163097" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y \\\\ (x-y)^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)=2xy,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2})=2(x-y),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2})=-2(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163097/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163097"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162941"] :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy \\\\ {e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy)=2y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy)=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})=y{e}^{xy},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})=x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163099/selection/7affc80b354d5672e5846ec2848bc72acc917ab829c5d29c165dc0339c2345bb" :answer/id #uuid "443b6a1c-a9be-589e-83c0-8a1140e70862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {e}^{x-y} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163099/selection/a2402970a6e90893abe7f6354e75c83e167ba8dee3bec22815ae36613751a959" :answer/id #uuid "5fa2ce42-b90b-54f1-a3a2-eb4d781ac2ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ -y{e}^{x-y} & x{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163099/selection/7c72e4950cfaf9fafbcbeb92c1770059dd8afb96d905c46f1f3f03925d95bd7f" :answer/id #uuid "d6f559c7-2497-5d3b-916b-fa64f3555eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ 