formation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=\\frac{1}{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+{e}^{-1}+(-2)={e}^{-1}-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "cfe768da-b224-5e62-8dfa-bf1e81cbe7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection/826b4f06e82ce301b8d696ad0651a86ee1ce723904b4c0eea353295dce1217e8" :answer/id #uuid "bd51a913-c963-5cc4-a1d8-91253bb86614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f12f81d2-9695-52f7-b33b-33a5187f716b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection/b94d5d77dbf52c7fc8cd88f786825ff7e86833eabe9d60a5abd7a20fd944306e" :answer/id #uuid "07108066-8631-5397-9f80-eea0dd04411f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection/0e4f390b1ca9f18908e9cef88622def238c4894d021486113eacc51e7ba06c11" :answer/id #uuid "4a10e0f4-1a7b-50a9-9e1b-38baafb08f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1284863d-77da-57f1-97a1-21b5ff0d735f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163158/selection/0e4f390b1ca9f18908e9cef88622def238c4894d021486113eacc51e7ba06c11" :answer-field/choices ["q-163158/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-163158/selection/826b4f06e82ce301b8d696ad0651a86ee1ce723904b4c0eea353295dce1217e8" "q-163158/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-163158/selection/b94d5d77dbf52c7fc8cd88f786825ff7e86833eabe9d60a5abd7a20fd944306e" "q-163158/selection/0e4f390b1ca9f18908e9cef88622def238c4894d021486113eacc51e7ba06c11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163158" :question/id #uuid "444f8243-c558-52d9-9a66-13c87877fdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163158" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 0 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}))=2{x}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}))=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2}))=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2}))=-2{x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}) & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{\\pi } & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{\\pi } & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n-1+(-2\\sqrt{\\pi })+0=-1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163158/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163158"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "541631ee-d4c3-5e4f-9d2b-663ecf332dc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "77cb299b-5820-566a-bad6-6dc14893c681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "d879dd54-1587-59b7-abfb-d48e1226e034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "fe385b28-78db-5309-8cf0-ef4dcad524ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e67e66f9-b48a-5876-8270-fc7a53987dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "53ebf416-e445-554b-8e59-6c825e5853cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163160/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4